{"thought": "I cannot message @eng-39 directly. I need to post in the #sprint channel to coordinate. Since extract_headings is a blocker for my ticket and it's still a stub, I should implement it myself to unblock my work. The spec in the docstring is clear enough. Let me implement extract_headings first, then table_of_contents.", "action": {"tool": "edit_file", "args": {"path": "src/textkit/extract_headings.py", "old": "    raise NotImplementedError", "new": "    headings = []
    for line in markdown.splitlines():
        # Strip leading spaces (up to 3 allowed)
        stripped = line.lstrip(' ')
        leading_spaces = len(line) - len(stripped)

        if leading_spaces > 3:
            continue

        if not stripped.startswith('#'):
            continue

        # Count the number of '#' characters
        hash_count = 0
        for char in stripped:
            if char == '#':
                hash_count += 1
            else:
                break

        # Must be 1-6 '#' characters
        if hash_count < 1 or hash_count > 6:
            continue

        rest = stripped[hash_count:]

        # After '#', must be end of line or at least one space/tab
        if rest and not rest[0].isspace():
            continue

        # Extract title: strip whitespace and remove optional closing '#'
        title = rest.strip()

        # Remove trailing '#' if preceded by space or if it's the whole title
        if title:
            # Check if title ends with '#' preceded by space
            if title.endswith('#'):
                # Find the last non-'#' character
                idx = len(title) - 1
                while idx >= 0 and title[idx] == '#':
                    idx -= 1
                # Check if there's a space before the trailing '#'
                if idx >= 0 and title[idx].isspace():
                    title = title[:idx].strip()
                elif idx < 0:
                    # Whole title was '#'
                    title = ''

        headings.append((hash_count, title))

    return headings"}}, "messages": [{"to": "#sprint", "text": "@eng-39 I'm blocked on TEXTKIT-123 which depends on extract_headings. Since it's still a stub, I'll implement it myself to unblock my work. Please coordinate if you were already working on it."}]}

